A note on why the prose is open, given what this repository is.

The cases here describe failures. Some of them, eventually, will describe
failures in systems made by people who would prefer the description not exist.
If the text were "all rights reserved", those people would have a legal argument
that quoting a case to rebut them is infringement — and the cheap way to win
that argument is to make the list too expensive to cite. CC BY removes the
argument. Attribution is the only thing asked in return, and the case files are
written to be citable: each one carries its own verdict, provenance and witness.

What CC BY does NOT grant: it does not license any third party's system, log,
trademark, or data that a submission happens to quote. Contributors are
responsible for having the right to publish their trace (see the checklist in
templates/submission-template.md).
